<Layout title="Privacy and website use" description="How SamkhyaAcademy handles program enquiries, contact information and website use."><PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Your information matters." description="How we use the information you choose to share."/><section class="container section prose narrow"><h2>Browsing and enquiries</h2><p>The program enquiry and venture idea pages embed academy-owned Google Apps Script forms. Submitted fields are saved in the academy’s private Google Sheet so authorised staff can review your request and respond. Google provides form hosting, storage and reCAPTCHA services. Read the notice and separate terms and consent acknowledgements before submitting.</p><h2>What we collect and why</h2><p>The enquiry form asks for your name, email, mobile number, education or professional background, learning interests and question. We also record your enquiry reference, receipt time and policy acknowledgements. Venture briefs also ask for your idea, intended users, stage, proposed approach, evidence and support needs. These support program or advisory discussions, follow-up and reliable handling of your request. Program enquiries and venture ideas are kept in separate private workbooks.</p><h2>Access and sharing</h2><p>Access is limited through private account and file permissions to authorised people managing academy enquiries. We do not sell enquiry information or share it for unrelated marketing. Sharing a venture brief with an external adviser requires separate permission. No online service can promise absolute security; keep an initial message non-confidential.</p><h2>Correction, deletion and retention</h2><p>Email contact@samkhyaacademy.com to request correction or deletion of your enquiry information. We keep information only for the enquiry or engagement and applicable record-keeping needs, and review inactive records for removal. Active engagements may have separately agreed retention terms. Removal from active records may not immediately remove copies held in service backups or version history.</p><h2>Contacting the academy</h2><p>You can contact the academy by email, phone or WhatsApp. Your contact information and message are used to respond to your request and discuss relevant learning or advisory arrangements. Please share only what is needed for that conversation. WhatsApp and email are external services with their own privacy practices. For questions about your information, email <a href="mailto:contact@samkhyaacademy.com">contact@samkhyaacademy.com</a>.</p><h2>Sharing links</h2><p>Sharing controls let you copy a page link or choose an external sharing service. Opening an external service is subject to that service’s privacy practices.</p><h2>Information you share</h2><p>Do not include passwords, identity documents, private customer data or confidential material in an initial enquiry.</p><p>See the <a href="/terms/">website terms</a>.</p></section></Layout>
